@*
    Export, import and factory reset, on a page of their own.

    The three operations here act on the whole server rather than on a row, and two of them can
    replace or delete everything on it — so they are reachable deliberately, by the operator
    account only (AdminController.IsOperator), and never as panels scrolled past on the way to
    something else.

    The page decides nothing itself. Import is two API calls: analyse, which works out every
    mode against the database as it is and says which rows each one would insert, update, skip
    or exclude and why; then apply, with the mode the operator picked and the hash of the plan
    they were shown. A script driving the same API gets the same answers this page draws.

    Self-contained for the same reason Manage.cshtml is: a view rendered out of a NuGet package
    cannot assume the host has a layout, a _ViewStart or tag helpers.
*@
@{
    Layout = null;
    var tenant = ViewBag.Tenant as Ark.oAuth.ArkTenant;
    var title = tenant?.display ?? tenant?.name ?? (ViewBag.TenantId as string);
    var allowImport = ViewBag.AllowImport == true;
    var allowReset = ViewBag.AllowReset == true;
}
<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="en">
<head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta name="robots" content="noindex, nofollow" />
    <meta name="referrer" content="strict-origin" />
    <title>Data — @title</title>
    <link href="@ViewBag.ConsoleCss" rel="stylesheet" />
</head>
<body>
@await Html.PartialAsync("_ConsoleHeader")

<main class="ark-main"
      id="ark-admin"
      data-page="data"
      data-app-root="@ViewBag.AppRoot"
      data-tenant-id="@ViewBag.TenantId"
      data-operator-tenant="@ViewBag.OperatorTenant"
      data-user-password-mode="@ViewBag.UserPasswordMode"
      data-allow-import="@(allowImport.ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
      data-allow-replace="@((ViewBag.AllowReplace == true).ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
      data-allow-reset="@(allowReset.ToString().ToLowerInvariant())"
      data-sign-out-url="@ViewBag.SignOutUrl">

    @*
        What is on the server now, by table and category. The same four categories are the
        choices on the import panel, so the operator can see what "grants" or "history" means in
        rows before deciding whether to bring them across.
    *@
    <section class="ark-panel">
        <div class="ark-panel-head">
            <h2>This server</h2>
            <span class="ark-hint">every table the identity server keeps, and how many rows each holds</span>
            <span class="ark-spacer"></span>
            <button type="button" class="ark-btn-ghost ark-btn-sm" id="dt-refresh">Refresh</button>
        </div>
        <div class="ark-panel-body">
            <div class="ark-data-counts" id="dt-counts"><p class="ark-empty">Loading…</p></div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @*
        Export. Every mapped table and column — including the password hashes, client secret
        hashes and private signing keys the management API never returns — so the file is as
        sensitive as the database. Hence the passphrase: AES-256-GCM, applied on the server, with
        nothing about the key stored anywhere.
    *@
    <section class="ark-panel">
        <div class="ark-panel-head">
            <h2>Export</h2>
            <span class="ark-hint">tenants, clients, users, mappings, signing keys, scopes, claims, grants, history and app settings — one JSON file</span>
        </div>
        <div class="ark-panel-body">
            <div class="ark-alert ark-alert-warn">
                The file holds every private signing key and password hash on this server. Anyone holding it can sign
                tokens as this identity provider. Encrypt it, and keep it where you keep database backups.
            </div>
            <div class="ark-grid-2">
                <div class="ark-field">
                    <label for="ex-passphrase">Passphrase</label>
                    <input type="password" id="ex-passphrase" autocomplete="new-password" placeholder="leave blank for a plain JSON file" />
                    <div class="ark-note">Needed again to import the file. It is not stored anywhere and cannot be recovered.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="ark-field">
                    <label for="ex-passphrase2">Passphrase, again</label>
                    <input type="password" id="ex-passphrase2" autocomplete="new-password" />
                </div>
            </div>
            <div class="ark-check">
                <input type="checkbox" id="ex-secrets" />
                <label for="ex-secrets">Include secret app settings (passwords, client secrets, connection strings) instead of redacting them</label>
            </div>
            <div class="ark-provision-actions">
                <button type="button" id="ex-submit">Download export</button>
                <span class="ark-note" style="margin:0">App settings are exported for reference: an import compares them with this server's but never changes configuration.</span>
            </div>
        </div>
    </section>

    @if (allowImport)
    {
        @*
            Import. Analyse first: the server works out all three modes against the database as it
            is now, and the operator picks one with the consequences in front of them. Rows the
            server cannot load safely are excluded by rule, not by guess, and each one says which
            rule — the same file against the same database always gives the same plan.
        *@
        <section class="ark-panel">
            <div class="ark-panel-head">
                <h2>Import</h2>
                <span class="ark-hint">analyse a file, choose how to load it, then load it in one transaction</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ark-panel-body">
                <div class="ark-grid-2">
                    <div class="ark-field">
                        <label for="im-file">Export file</label>
                        <input type="file" id="im-file" accept=".json,application/json" />
                        <div class="ark-note" id="im-file-note">Read in this browser and sent to the server as JSON.</div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ark-field" id="im-passphrase-field" hidden>
                        <label for="im-passphrase">Passphrase <span class="ark-req">encrypted file</span></label>
                        <input type="password" id="im-passphrase" autocomplete="off" />
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ark-field">
                    <label>Load these categories</label>
                    <div class="ark-check-row" id="im-include">
                        <span class="ark-check"><input type="checkbox" id="im-cat-configuration" value="configuration" checked disabled /><label for="im-cat-configuration">configuration</label></span>
                        <span class="ark-check"><input type="checkbox" id="im-cat-grants" value="grants" checked /><label for="im-cat-grants">grants <span class="ark-hint">sessions, refresh tokens, consents</span></label></span>
                        <span class="ark-check"><input type="checkbox" id="im-cat-transient" value="transient" checked /><label for="im-cat-transient">transient <span class="ark-hint">codes still in flight</span></label></span>
                        <span class="ark-check"><input type="checkbox" id="im-cat-history" value="history" checked /><label for="im-cat-history">history <span class="ark-hint">audit trail, sign-in counters</span></label></span>
                        <span class="ark-check"><input type="checkbox" id="im-cat-other" value="other" checked /><label for="im-cat-other">other</label></span>
                    </div>
                    <div class="ark-note">Configuration is always loaded — everything else points at it. Changing a box needs a new analysis.</div>
                </div>
                <div class="ark-check" id="im-modified-field" hidden>
                    <input type="checkbox" id="im-allow-modified" />
                    <label for="im-allow-modified">The file was edited after export on purpose — import it anyway</label>
                </div>
                <div class="ark-provision-actions">
                    <button type="button" id="im-analyse" disabled>Analyse</button>
                    <span class="ark-note" style="margin:0">Nothing is written until you choose a mode and press Import.</span>
                </div>

                <div id="im-analysis" class="ark-import" hidden></div>
            </div>
        </section>
    }

    @if (allowReset)
    {
        @*
            Factory reset. Deletes every row in every table and runs the seed a brand-new database
            gets, in one transaction — the schema and its migration history are kept, so the server
            is current, just empty. The server checks the seed can run (an administrator password is
            configured) before deleting anything; the panel shows that check up front.
        *@
        <section class="ark-panel ark-panel-danger">
            <div class="ark-panel-head">
                <h2>Factory reset</h2>
                <span class="ark-hint">delete everything and start again from the first-run seed</span>
            </div>
            <div class="ark-panel-body">
                <ul class="ark-list">
                    <li>Every tenant, client, user, mapping, signing key, scope edit, session, token and audit row is deleted.</li>
                    <li>The server then seeds itself exactly as a new install does: tenant <code>@ViewBag.OperatorTenant</code>, its admin console and machine clients, a new signing key, the standard scopes and claims, and the administrator account.</li>
                    <li>The administrator password goes back to the one configured in <code>ark_oauth_server:AdminUser:Password</code>. Every application has to be registered again.</li>
                </ul>
                <div class="ark-alert" id="rs-seed-problem" hidden></div>
                <div class="ark-grid-2">
                    <div class="ark-field">
                        <label for="rs-confirm">Type <code>@ViewBag.OperatorTenant</code> to confirm</label>
                        <input type="text" id="rs-confirm" autocomplete="off" spellcheck="false" />
                    </div>
                </div>
                <div class="ark-check">
                    <input type="checkbox" id="rs-backup" checked />
                    <label for="rs-backup">Download an export of everything first</label>
                </div>
                <div class="ark-provision-actions">
                    <button type="button" class="ark-btn-danger-solid" id="rs-submit" disabled>Reset this server</button>
                </div>
                <div id="rs-result"></div>
            </div>
        </section>
    }
</main>

<div class="ark-toasts" id="ark-toasts" aria-live="polite"></div>

<script src="@ViewBag.ConsoleJs"></script>
</body>
</html>
